{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Thus.</b> He made all; I do all My will. And the witness: \"I stretched out the heavens alone.\"" "<b>From Me.</b> By My power, for HaShem is not a body. And it is written, \"Who is with Me?\" and behold, it is like \"alone.\" And know that Scripture says \"who stretches out the heavens and spreads out the earth,\" for their standing is continually by HaShem."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:02.376259460Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}